# Week 3 — Requirements Analysis, Specification & Quality

## 1. Requirements Analysis — CARS Matrix
The purpose of requirements analysis is to turn vague stakeholder statements into clear, verifiable requirements. All targets marked "proposed" need stakeholder confirmation.
Original statement | Diagnosis | Refined requirement | Type | Open question 

Volunteers need to register quickly. | "Quickly" is vague. | FR01: The system shall allow a volunteer to create an account. | Functional | Which personal information is required? 
Volunteers need to provide their information. | "Information" is unspecified. | FR02: The system shall allow a registered volunteer to record and update their skills and availability. | Functional | Which skills and availability details are needed?
Volunteers need to upload documents. | Which documents? Who checks them? | FR03: The system shall allow a volunteer to upload evidence of their qualifications. | Functional | Which file types are accepted? 
We need a calendar that everyone can see. | "Everyone" is ambiguous. | FR08: The system shall allow a volunteer to view upcoming events that need volunteers. | Functional | Which event details are public? 
Volunteers need to apply for events. | Application process not described. | FR09: The system shall allow a registered volunteer to submit an application for a role at an event. | Functional | Can a volunteer apply for several roles? 
Organisers manage events. | Several actions combined. | FR04: The system shall allow an authorised organiser to create, edit and cancel events and volunteer roles. | Functional | Who is authorised to cancel an event? 
Roles have limits and prerequisites. | Combined in one sentence. | FR10: The system shall allow an authorised organiser to set a capacity and qualification prerequisites for each role. | Functional | What counts as a prerequisite? 
Check if volunteers are vetted. | "Vetted" is unclear. | FR05: The system shall restrict applications for designated roles to volunteers whose required qualifications are recorded as verified. | Functional | Who verifies? What if pending or expired? 
Volunteers must know about changes. | Which changes and how? | FR06: The system shall notify volunteers registered for an event when that event is cancelled or its details change. | Functional | Which channel is acceptable? 
Organisers need volunteer lists. | Several actions combined. | FR07: The system shall allow an authorised organiser to view and confirm the volunteer roster for an assigned event. | Functional | When must rosters be finalised? 
Organisers may want lists outside the system. | Not supported by the scenario. | FR11 (candidate): The system shall allow an authorised organiser to export a roster. | Functional | Is export needed at all? 
The system must be easy to use. | "Easy" is not measurable. | NFR01: In a usability test, at least 90% of first-time volunteers shall find an event and submit an application within 3 minutes without assistance. | Usability | Who are representative users? 
The system must be fast. | No operation, load or time. | NFR02: With 25 concurrent users, at least 95% of event searches shall return results within 2 seconds. | Performance | What is the real peak load? 
Volunteer data must be protected. | No asset, no who. | NFR03: Volunteer phone numbers and email addresses shall be visible only to authorised users who need them for their assigned role. | Security / Privacy | Who is authorised? 
The system must be available. | No window. | NFR04: During agreed operating hours each month, registration shall be available at least 99.5% of the time, measured by agreed monitoring. | Availability | What are the operating hours? 

The numbers in NFR01, NFR02 and NFR04 are **proposed**, not agreed.

## 2. MoSCoW Prioritisation
These priorities are provisional and require stakeholder confirmation.

Priority | Items | Reason 

Must | FR01, FR02, FR04, FR08, FR09 | Without registration, events and applications the core service does not work. 
Must (provisional) | FR05 | Core safety rule, but depends on the open question of who verifies qualifications. 
Should | FR03, FR06, FR07, FR10 | Important; an organiser-managed workaround may exist, to be confirmed. 
Could | FR11 (export), calendar view (candidate), waitlist (candidate) | Not supported by the scenario; need decisions. 
Won't (this release) | None assigned | No stakeholder has confirmed any exclusion. 

Dependency: FR05 needs verified status to be recorded. Whether FR03 (upload) is the way to do this, or an authorised person records it, is an open question.

